# Line endings are part of the build contract (a0-64).
#
# Several tests compare a committed artifact, read off disk, against a string
# built in memory — which always uses "\n":
#
#   src/art/preview.test.ts   assets/preview/sprite-sheet.svg vs buildContactSheet()
#   tests/codex/tone-mirror.test.ts   GDD.md sliced at literal "\n\n" markers
#
# Without this file, checkout line endings are decided by whatever `core.autocrlf`
# the cloning machine happens to carry. A CRLF checkout rewrites every one of those
# committed bytes on its way to disk, so the comparison can never match and main
# goes red on a tree that is byte-for-byte correct in the repository. Pinning LF on
# checkout makes the working tree agree with the index on every machine.
#
# Every text blob in this repo is already LF, so this changes no committed content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never inspected, never converted.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.woff2 binary

# The one committed text file with mixed endings. Left exactly as it is so a fresh
# clone does not report it as modified; it is a captured probe log, not source.
evidence/images/probe-online-live-recheck2-m10.txt -text
